775:     /**
776:      * Implementations of this method should register/unregister the fig for all
777:      * (model)events. For FigEdgeModelElement only the fig itself is registered
778:      * as listening to events fired by the owner itself. But for, for example,
779:      * FigAssociation the fig must also register for events fired by the
780:      * stereotypes of the owner. <p>
781:      * 
782:      * This function is used in UMLDiagram, which removes all listeners 
783:      * to all Figs when a diagram is not displayed, and restore them
784:      * when it becomes visible again. <p>
785:      * 
786:      * In this case, it is not imperative that indeed ALL listeners are 
787:      * updated, as long as the ones removed get added again and vice versa. <p>
788:      * 
789:      * Additionally, this function may be used by the modelChanged() function.
790:      * <p>
791:      * 
792:      * In this case, it IS imperative that all listeners get removed / added.
793:      * 
794:      * @param newOwner the new owner for the listeners
795:      */
796:     protected void updateListeners(Object newOwner) {
797:         Object oldOwner = getOwner();
798:         if (oldOwner != null) {
799:             removeElementListener(oldOwner);
800:         }
801:         if (newOwner != null) {
802:             addElementListener(newOwner);
803:         }
804:     }
