Has the original ask been met?  
No. The file still declares and uses the old methods `getAllModelElementsOfKind(...)` and never introduces or calls a new `getAllModelElementsOfKindWithModel(...)` that takes both a model and a type.  

What needs to change:  
1) Rename the zero‐model wrapper  
   • At line 162 the method  
       public Collection getAllModelElementsOfKind(Object type)  
     should be changed to something like  
       public Collection getAllModelElementsOfKindWithModel(Object model, Object type)  
     and its body adapted to use the passed‐in `model` rather than fetching it via the ProjectManager.  

2) Rename the recursive helper  
   • At line 188 the method  
       public Collection getAllModelElementsOfKind(Object nsa, Object type)  
     needs to be renamed to match the new public API, e.g.  
       public Collection getAllModelElementsOfKindWithModel(Object model, Object nsa, Object type)  
     and internal recursive calls updated accordingly.  

3) Update all call sites to the old name  
   • Line 168:  
       Collection ret = getAllModelElementsOfKind(model, kind);  
     must become  
       Collection ret = getAllModelElementsOfKindWithModel(model, model, kind);  
     (or adapted to your final signature)  
   • Line 227:  
       Collection elementsCol1 = getAllModelElementsOfKind(element, kind);  
     must become  
       Collection elementsCol1 = getAllModelElementsOfKindWithModel(model, element, kind);  
   • Line 305:  
       Collection classifiers = getAllModelElementsOfKind(ns, ModelFacade.CLASSIFIER);  
     must become  
       Collection classifiers = getAllModelElementsOfKindWithModel(model, ns, ModelFacade.CLASSIFIER);  

4) Likewise rename and fix the String‐based overload at lines 260–278, and any other occurrences.

The task is INCOMPLETE.

