360:     /**
361:      * Finds the absolute path of a ModelElement. Ie the name of each
362:      * namespace starting at the root (the Model) and ending with the
363:      * name of the element.<p>
364:      *
365:      * The returned Vector implicitly starts at the root (the model)
366:      * and follows element's chain of owning namespaces back down to
367:      * element. The first element will thus be the name of the top level
368:      * namespace below the model, and the last element will be the name
369:      * of element itself. Note thus that for the model the path will be
370:      * empty.
371:      *
372:      * @param  element is the object to resolve the path for.
373:      * @return A Vector as described above.
374:      * @throws IllegalArgumentException if element isn't a ModelElement
375:      *         properly owned by namespaces and a model.
376:      */
377:     public Vector getPath(Object element) {
378:         Vector path;
379: 
380:         if (ModelFacade.isAModel(element)) {
381:             return new Vector();
382:         }
383: 
384:         path = getPath(ModelFacade.getNamespace(element));
385:         path.add(ModelFacade.getName(element));
386: 
387:         return path;
388:     }
