390:     /**
391:      * Utility function for managing several overlayed models, eg a user
392:      * model to which elements from some profile models is imported when
393:      * needed. This version of the function assumes it is permissible to
394:      * create missing elements.
395:      *
396:      * This function may fail and return null eg if some required object
397:      * doesn't exist in the target model and cannot be copied.
398:      *
399:      * @param elem is some element.
400:      * @param model is the model the returned object shall belong to.
401:      * @return An element of the same type and at the same position in the
402:      *  model as elem, or if that would turn out impossible then null.
403:      */
404:     public Object getCorrespondingElement(Object elem, Object model) {
405:     return getCorrespondingElement(elem, model, true);
406:     }
